WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:10.600
You know, in CSGO, no matter how far behind you are, no matter how bad the round is looking,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:16.460
nothing tilts the enemy team off the
face of the earth better than a good ninja defuse.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:22.100
I’m Colin for theScore esports and whether you're sneaking behind enemy lines for a last second defuse,

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.740
Or going for that ballsy last ditch smoke ninja.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.520
I feel like I can watch these plays all day.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.360
So lets do just that and sneak into it, with the Top 10 Ninja Defuses in CS:GO.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.920
Kicking off our list at number 10 is a cheeky play from Dupreeh, who hides on Nuke’s B-site

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:49.900
before sneaking into an enemy smoke for a play that left LDLC rethinking the meaning of life.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:01:14.580
(Casting)

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.640
At Number 9 we have one of the first 1v5 ninja defuses in CS:GO.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.600
After disposing of four CLG players, it seemed like an easy round win for NRG,

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.540
but Tarik had other ideas.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:53.680
(Casting)

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:00.300
Coming in at number 8 is a play from Happy who just says, screw it, as he goes in for

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:07.400
a gutsy defuse in the smoke right next to ChrisJ, leading to an unlikely round win for EnVyUs.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:26.260
(Casting)

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.780
Our Number 7 spot goes to K0nfig.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:36.060
Up 12-4 against Fnatic in the Quarterfinals of Epicenter: Moscow, the Dane was looking

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:42.240
to add some salt to the wound as he sneaks behind enemy lines to pull off a clutch for  the ages.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:03:18.460
(Casting)

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:25.560
At number 6 we’ve got Jaxi in the finals of Adria Masters Season 2.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:32.460
Down 12-7 to Bajini Pulenii, Nexus were looking for anything to get them team back in the game.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:40.160
Jaxi delivered exactly that, with this slick 1v5 ninja to start an overtime comeback win.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:04:07.520
(Casting)

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:13.220
Our next ninja defuse comes from PENTA’’s Tabsen, who plays a game of cat and mouse,

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:20.560
before pouncing on the perfect opportunity for a sick 1v4 ninja defuse to win the round.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:54.960
(Casting)

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:59.200
Coming in at Number 4 is a 200 IQ play from Devil.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:05.000
Faced with a 1v3, he jukes out the members of FaZe clan with this unbelievable clutch

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:10.240
that saw him fake an AWP save, before coming back for a last second defuse

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:54.460
(Casting)

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:58.640
Sneaking in at number 3 is Kjaerbye at Dreamhack Malmo.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:04.080
After losing 4 teammates, Kjaerbye was looking for the hero play, as he hid in construction

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:12.920
on Inferno’s B site to pull off an incredible 1v5 ninja that would tilt EnVyUs off the face of the Earth.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:44.840
(Casting)

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:54.480
Taking the runner up spot is the Polish legend himself at IEM Katowice 2016.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:59.980
In a round that seemed impossible to win for Virtus.pro, Snax turned it all around with

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.480
this ninja defuse in a 1v5 situation against FaZe Clan.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:47.150
Capping off our list at number 1 is none other
than Krimz, who shows us, he is an actual

00:07:47.150 --> 00:08:15.240
ninja as he evades 5 TSM players

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:31.550
for 
a

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:45.890
ninja defuse 
to remember.

